# WorkResolve environment configuration — copy to .env.local and fill in.
# NEVER commit .env.local (or any file with real values) — see .gitignore.
# NEVER put a private key, seed phrase, or API secret in a NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# variable: everything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is bundled into client-side
# JavaScript and is publicly visible to anyone who loads the app.

# --- GenLayer network -------------------------------------------------------

# The app now has an in-UI network switcher (see src/hooks/useNetwork.tsx,
# src/components/layout/NetworkSwitcher.tsx) — added after a real, confirmed
# GenLayer Asimov Testnet liveness incident on 2026-09-08 (see
# docs/limitations.md). A person's choice in that switcher is persisted per
# browser (localStorage) and ALWAYS wins over the setting below once made.
#
# This variable only sets the *seed* default — what a first-time visitor to
# this build sees before they've picked anything. One of:
#   localnet          - GenLayer Studio running locally (chain id 61127) —
#                        not offered in the in-app switcher, dev-only
#   studionet          - hosted GenLayer Studio, no local setup required (chain id 61999)
#   testnetAsimov      - public GenLayer testnet (chain id 4221)
#   testnetBradbury    - public GenLayer testnet (chain id 4221)
# Defaults to "studionet" if unset — deliberately, for the reliability
# reason above (Studio is centrally operated and doesn't depend on real
# validator liveness the way the public testnets do). Re-verify network
# identities against https://docs.genlayer.com before a real deployment —
# testnet identity has changed before.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GENLAYER_NETWORK=studionet

# Optional: override the RPC endpoint for the selected network above.
# Leave unset to use the network's default endpoint.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GENLAYER_RPC_URL=

# --- WorkResolve contract ----------------------------------------------------

# Each network above has its OWN deployed contract address — a deployment on
# Studio and one on Asimov are unrelated addresses on unrelated networks,
# never the same contract. Set the address for every network you actually
# want to work in the switcher; a network with no address configured shows a
# clear "not deployed on this network yet" error instead of crashing (see
# src/lib/genlayer/config.ts's requireContractAddress()).
#
# PUTTING ONE NETWORK'S ADDRESS IN ANOTHER NETWORK'S VARIABLE COSTS A DAY —
# it happened here on 2026-09-09 (see docs/limitations.md). Nothing fails at
# build time, reads can keep working against whichever network the address
# really belongs to, and some wallets report the resulting write failure as
# nothing more useful than "an internal error". Before pasting an address
# below, confirm it resolves on THAT network's own explorer:
#   studionet     -> https://explorer-studio.genlayer.com/address/<addr>
#   testnetAsimov -> https://explorer-asimov.genlayer.com/address/<addr>
# And when deploying, check the active network in the SAME shell first
# (`genlayer config get`) — a `genlayer network set` run in another terminal
# does not apply to yours.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKRESOLVE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_STUDIONET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKRESOLVE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_TESTNET_ASIMOV=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKRESOLVE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_TESTNET_BRADBURY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKRESOLVE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS_LOCALNET=

# Legacy, unsuffixed variable — kept working as a fallback for
# testnetAsimov ONLY (this project's original single-network variable,
# already configured on this project's Vercel deployment before the
# multi-network switcher existed). Prefer the _TESTNET_ASIMOV form above for
# any new setup; this one is read only if that specific one is unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKRESOLVE_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# --- Evidence storage (IPFS) --------------------------------------------------

# Server-side only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) — used by the future
# /api/ipfs/upload route (see docs/architecture.md section 9). Not yet
# implemented in Phase 3; documented here so the shape is decided ahead of
# time. Never expose this key to the browser.
# IPFS_PINNING_API_KEY=
# IPFS_PINNING_API_SECRET=
